drm/apple: tag RGB planes on the internal panel as sRGB

667ca85b1804 made get_colorspace() return BG_SRGB for RGB planes, so DCP
maps them from sRGB into the panel's native gamut; NATIVE on the P3 MacBook
panels gives oversaturated colours. e49109f8b7b2 ("drm/apple: Only assume RGB
planes on internal displays are sRGB", 5067ac875081 on the asahi tags)
reverted that line and added an eDP check that turns BG_SRGB into NATIVE on
the internal panel, the opposite of its subject and comment. Every RGB plane
on every connector has been NATIVE since asahi-6.18.7-1 and the eDP branch is
dead code. Return BG_SRGB for RGB planes again and send NATIVE to external
displays only, as that commit describes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -1361,7 +1361,7 @@
 		 * the contained colorimetry information to provide native
 		 * colors.
 		 */
-		if (dcp->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP &&
+		if (dcp->connector_type != DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP &&
 		    req->surf[l].base.colorspace == DCP_COLORSPACE_BG_SRGB)
 			req->surf[l].base.colorspace = DCP_COLORSPACE_NATIVE;
 	}
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/plane.c
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@
 					  enum drm_color_encoding enc)
 {
 	if (!is_yuv)
-		return DCP_COLORSPACE_NATIVE;
+		return DCP_COLORSPACE_BG_SRGB;
 
 	switch (enc) {
 	case DRM_COLOR_YCBCR_BT601:
